id: pm-y0htkd
title: "MCP update keys and CLI update flags diverge in name (linkedFile/linkedTest vs --file/--test), so an agent that reads the MCP contract and writes a CLI command produces a guaranteed unknown-option refusal"
description: Unify MCP update keys and CLI update flags through the shared contract vocabulary so linkedFile and linkedTest resolve to accepted CLI spellings or registered aliases. Add cross-surface parity enforcement and actionable unknown-option recovery without removing either capability.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,"area:contracts","area:mcp",cross-surface-parity,defect-recurrence
created_at: "2026-08-10T05:53:35.894Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-18T12:14:09.394Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-18T12:14:08.496Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-18T12:14:08.496Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "Every MCP declared key resolves to a CLI flag, via a shared name or a registered alias; A parity gate fails when an MCP declared key has no CLI flag or alias that accepts it; The unknown-option recovery names the accepted flag for a known cross-surface synonym"
parent: pm-5k4v
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: medium
repro_steps: "1. Read the pm_update declared keys, which list linkedFile and linkedTest  2. Run pm update <id> --linked-file path=a.ts  3. Refusal: Unknown option --linked-file"
resolution: "The SDK exports deterministic MCP-to-CLI and positional-action flag parity; all 43 create parameters and all 48 update parameters remain executable with zero findings, and structured help folds linked-resource aliases into their canonical options."
expected_result: "One name per concept across MCP and CLI, or an alias so a contract-derived name always parses."
actual_result: Mixed --file/--linked-file and --test/--linked-test values survive create and update losslessly; JSON help publishes the alias spellings; exact unknown-option acceptance proves malformed --linked-files is rejected.
component: "mcp/server, sdk/cli-contracts, commands/update"
