comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-18T04:52:00.566Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-18: one coupled SDK/CLI/MCP tranche will make positional actions and recovery references contract-declared, executable, parity-gated, and discoverable. Scope includes generated contracts, public SDK types, CLI help and recovery, MCP aliases, assurance negative controls, documentation, temporary-workspace acceptance, and packed npm/Bun consumers. Duplicate check used the complete 2,521-item all-status corpus with zero omissions or truncation."
  "2026-08-18T06:29:32.670Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: command grammar assurance proves MCP-to-CLI option parity for all 43 create and 48 update parameters with zero findings; packed npm/npx and Bun/bunx consumers executed --linked-file and --linked-test mutations, Node and Bun narrow SDK imports, action help, and scoped contracts successfully."
  "2026-08-18T06:45:42.746Z","harness:codex","Closeout evidence: create/update linkedFile and linkedTest now map to executable --linked-file/--linked-test aliases and the exported SDK verifier reports zero parity findings across 43 create and 48 update parameters. PM-linked focused execution passed 21/21 tests; packed npx/bunx mutation acceptance and exact full coverage passed. The separate boolean flag_invocations residual is preserved under pm-pcy92t with precise discovered_from provenance."
  "2026-08-18T07:33:25.380Z","harness:codex","Review verification before close: 519 files and 7,542 tests passed at exact 100/100/100/100; MCP/CLI parity is zero findings for 43 create and 48 update parameters; ESLint, jscpd, SDK surface, static assurance, and packed/temp acceptance pass."
  "2026-08-18T08:04:18.258Z","harness:codex","Independent review start: preserve all values when canonical and alias repeatable flags are mixed, and make positional action accepted-flag derivation shared and fail closed."
  "2026-08-18T08:53:12.438Z","harness:codex","Final independent-review evidence: a fresh isolated tracker retained four files and four tests across mixed canonical/alias create+update invocations. Synthetic unknown accepted flags fail closed; MCP/CLI parity remains zero findings for 43 create and 48 update parameters. Exact 7,543-test coverage, pnpm lint, SDK surface, contracts, token gates, and transport floor pass."
  "2026-08-18T10:45:43.545Z","harness:codex","Late review implementation: alias descriptions now use the structured-help folding prefix; create/update JSON help expose --linked-file and --linked-test under the canonical options; the malformed plural negative control asserts code unknown_option plus exact rejected spelling. Focused verification passes 89/89."
  "2026-08-18T10:56:54.399Z","harness:codex","Final verification evidence: create/update structured help now proves canonical --file/--test flags publish --linked-file/--linked-test aliases; malformed --linked-files is parsed as code=unknown_option with the exact rejected spelling. The same full gate set passed, including 43 create and 48 update parameter parity and exact 100/100/100/100 repository coverage (53,124 lines; 55,035 statements; 11,369 functions; 41,062 branches)."
  "2026-08-18T12:14:00.631Z","harness:codex","Evidence: focused acceptance proves alias-only linkedFile/linkedTest arrays normalize to canonical file/test for both create and update, while empty canonical/alias arrays remain undefined. A disposable initialized project manually accepted --linked-file and --linked-test, and pm get --full returned the canonical file and test records. SDK/MCP parity remains green at 43 create and 48 update parameters."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-18T08:53:11.802Z","harness:codex",Repeatable aliases are independent Commander option buckets and must be concatenated rather than first-match selected; shared validated contract tables should use direct internal imports so public aggregate routing does not add cold-start work.
